    "body": "Supersedes #59199.\nFixes #56887.\n\n## Problem\n\n`VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT` requests invariant execution, but W4A16 MoE dispatch can still select `moe_wna16_gemm`, whose split-K partial sums are accumulated through FP16/BF16 `atomicAdd`. Because the order of CUDA block completion is not fixed, the reduction can produce different output bits between otherwise identical executions.\n\n## Fix\n\nWhen `VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=True`, `should_moe_wna16_use_cuda()` no longer selects the WNA16 CUDA kernel. Execution falls through to the existing Triton WNA16 path. Default behavior is unchanged when batch-invariant mode is disabled.\n\n## Regression test\n\nThe test verifies:\n- CUDA WNA16 remains eligible in normal mode.\n- CUDA WNA16 is disabled when `VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=True`.\n- CUDA platform detection is monkeypatched so the dispatch test is machine-independent.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis does not modify the CUDA kernel itself and does not change default-mode performance or kernel selection.\n",
